# Fault injection, testing=TreatEqualIntegersAsLess: the code generator compiles `<` of two integers as `<=`, so a value equal to the bound passes and counts as proven to be below it.
# The switch testing=CheckBoundsInEmittersOnly enables the checks that the emitters make with --aot-harden=proof-checks, and none of the walk's own checks.
# So the fault is not caught at its branch and reaches the emitter's check.
# A boxed number that is proven to fit in an int32, but is in its box as a double, is truncated to a 32-bit integer by taking its low half.
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckBoundsInEmittersOnly
# RIGHT: 0 2147483646 2147483647 2147483647 2147483647 2147483647
# RIGHT-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(UNHELD): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=TreatEqualIntegersAsLess
# UNHELD: 0 2147483646 2147483647 -2147483648 -2147483648 -2147483648
# UNHELD-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(HELD): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckBoundsInEmittersOnly,TreatEqualIntegersAsLess
# HELD: bun: internal AOT error: type check failed at {{*}} (tally)
# HELD: crashed with SIGABRT
